@startuml

!include ../../../../../../tooling/styles/plantuml/structural/component-diagram-style.iuml

title Subset Analysis: Computing Minimal Subsets via Transitive Closure

rectangle "**Auth UI**" as F $fill_caution
rectangle "**Auth Service**" as D $fill_ok
rectangle "**User Store**" as E $fill_ok
rectangle "**Crypto Lib**" as B $fill_primary
rectangle "**Logger**" as C $fill_primary
rectangle "**Config**" as A $fill_primary
rectangle "**Reporting**" as G $fill_caution
rectangle "**Report Engine**" as H $fill_ok

F -down-> D : <<uses>>
F -down-> C : <<uses>>
D -down-> E : <<uses>>
D -down-> B : <<uses>>
D -down-> C : <<uses>>
E -down-> A : <<uses>>
E -down-> C : <<uses>>
B -down-> A : <<uses>>
G -down-> H : <<uses>>
H -down-> E : <<uses>>
H -down-> C : <<uses>>

note as N1 $fill_dynamic
  **Minimal Subset for Auth UI**
  Transitive closure from Auth UI:
  {Auth UI, Auth Service, User Store,
   Crypto Lib, Logger, Config}
  All six modules must be present
  for Auth UI to function correctly.
end note

note as N2 $deep_caution
  **Minimal Subset for Reporting**
  Transitive closure from Reporting:
  {Reporting, Report Engine,
   User Store, Logger, Config}
  Five modules needed—note the
  overlap with Auth UI's subset.
end note
@enduml
